    "no": 4,
    "paper": "TECH1",
    "unit": "II",
    "sub": "Process Management",
    "q": "Which of the following is NOT one of the four necessary conditions for deadlock?",
    "opts": {
      "A": "Mutual exclusion",
      "B": "Hold and wait",
      "C": "Circular wait",
      "D": "Preemption"
    },
    "ans": "D",
    "exp": "The Coffman conditions are mutual exclusion, hold and wait, NO preemption, and circular wait. Preemption as stated is the opposite of the required condition — if resources can be preempted, deadlock is broken rather than caused. Watch the wording carefully: examiners flip \"no preemption\" to \"preemption\" precisely because candidates pattern-match on the word alone.",
    "conf": null,
    "prov": "Authored for MPSC JSO prep, reused here where the topic overlaps the System Manager syllabus. Not a past System Manager question.",
    "note": ""
